  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Maximus Federal Services obligated $430M in FY2026 to date. Maximus Federal Services won 47 awards in the current fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $9.1M. Obligations fell 71.0% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows $1.4B in FY21, $1.1B in FY22, $1.1B in FY23, $1.1B in FY24, and $1.5B in FY25. The Department of Health and Human Services is the largest buyer in FY2026 to date, obligating $229M. The Department of Education is the next largest buyer in FY2026 to date, obligating $143M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market in FY2026 to date, with $226M in obligations. Telemarketing Bureaus and Other Contact Centers is the second-largest market, with $129M in obligations. Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services accounts for $73.2M in FY2026 to date. This summary reflects fiscal year to date activity and partial-year totals for FY2026 only.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations fall 71.0% year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 71.0% year over year while FY2026 to date obligations stand at $430M. Prior fiscal years show larger full-year totals of $1.4B in FY21 and between $1.1B and $1.5B in FY22 through FY25. Concentration in a few large buyers and markets helps explain the shift: the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $229M and the Department of Education obligated $143M in FY2026 to date. Markets such as Computer Systems Design Services ($226M) and Telemarketing Bureaus and Other Contact Centers ($129M) account for most FY2026 to date obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are FY2026 to date dollars concentrated?",
        "body": "The Department of Health and Human Services leads FY2026 to date buying with $229M. The Department of Education follows with $143M in obligations. Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $226M and Telemarketing Bureaus and Other Contact Centers accounts for $129M in FY2026 to date. Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services adds $73.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
